  "note": [
    "v2 section 04, task 4.4. Routes laid out by hand over the committed golden",
    "trajectories in crates/sailgym-physics/tests/golden/*.json, and the passage",
    "sequences each one produces under the F15.3 rule. Generated once and then",
    "committed; crates/sailgym-course/tests/replay.rs reads it and asserts it.",
    "'sample' indexes the golden's samples array, 5 Hz, so t = sample / 5 s.",
    "'clearance_m' is the signed lateral offset of the boat from the mark at the",
    "crossing, along the leg's left normal: positive means the boat passed to",
    "port of the leg direction, so the mark was left to starboard, and the",
    "magnitude is how far clear of the mark it went. For a gate there is no side,",
    "so 'along_gate' gives the crossing's fractional position between the posts",
    "instead. Both are documentation of the hand-check, not assertions."
